What this file is for
---------------------

AGPL-3.0 section 5 requires that a modified work keep intact all notices
stating that it is licensed under this License, and that it carry prominent
notices stating that it is modified and the date. This file does both, and
records who holds what, because the repository's own history makes the answer
precise rather than a matter of assertion.

Adding a line here is how a derivative work claims its own authorship. It is
not a place to remove anyone else's.


Who wrote what
--------------

ZIRI PMS is a derivative of Kamra PMS (https://github.com/Kamra-PMS/kamra-pms),
an AGPL-3.0 hotel property-management system. The upstream work is the larger
part of this repository by a wide margin and its authorship is unchanged.

  Upstream (Kamra PMS)
    Mohammed Azzan and the Kamra/HeyKoala contributors.
    The application core: the front desk, folios and the ledger, the night
    audit, reservations and the booking engine, housekeeping, banquets, the
    POS, the agent layer, and the React console they are served through.
    Their copyright headers appear in the source files they wrote and are
    left exactly as they are.

  This distribution (ZIRI PMS — Algeria)
    Ilyes Keskas.
    The Algerian localization — TVA and the taxe de séjour, the NIF/RC/NIS/AI
    identifiers, the 58 wilayas and their communes, French and Arabic for the
    console; and the productization layer the hotel is actually run by: the
    installer and the Docker deployment, the backup and restore verifier with
    its negative controls and its systemd timers, the health checks, the error
    code taxonomy, the support bundle and its redaction, the installation
    identifier, monitoring and alerting, the entitlement record, and the
    update, rollback and disaster-recovery procedures.

The split is not an estimate. `git shortlog -sne` counts the commits, and
`git log --diff-filter=A` names who created each file; the files carrying an
"Ilyes Keskas" header are the ones that command attributes to him.


